(312247, 22792, 2989, '<td valign="top">Thanks to everyone for thier comments.  It is a shot of an extremely interesting exhibit at the Museum of Fine Arts, Houston.  The person standing in the shot is a lady who works there.  She stood very still and yelled at anyone who tried touching the walls.<br/> <br/>The tunnel of light looked so different it was interesting to see the results.  Also the light changes color, so I also had to decide what color to use.</td>', 'Thanks to everyone for thier comments.  It is a shot of an extremely interesting exhibit at the Museum of Fine Arts, Houston.  The person standing in the shot is a lady who works there.  She stood very still and yelled at anyone who tried touching the walls. The tunnel of light looked so different it was interesting to see the results.  Also the light changes color, so I also had to decide what color to use.', '2003-06-02 01:09:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(312248, 22627, 6325, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the encouraging comments. A little more about the picture.<br/> - It was taken at ground level.<br/> - I had been watching the thunderhead build for a coupls of hours and took shots now and then.<br/> - This is looking East.<br/> - About an hour before sunset, I moved out to the side of the house and setup on the tripod. You can sometimes get dramatic effects at the end of the day with the sun lighing just the top of the clouds.<br/> - I would snap a shot now and then. These thunderheads change minute to minute.<br/> - I heard the ducks quacking as they left the little pond by the house. They hung a left and past right in front of the camera. I got two shots since I was already setup on the tripod.<br/> <br/>Dennis</td>', 'Thanks for all the encouraging comments. A little more about the picture. - It was taken at ground level. - I had been watching the thunderhead build for a coupls of hours and took shots now and then. - This is looking East. - About an hour before sunset, I moved out to the side of the house and setup on the tripod. You can sometimes get dramatic effects at the end of the day with the sun lighing just the top of the clouds. - I would snap a shot now and then. These thunderheads change minute to minute. - I heard the ducks quacking as they left the little pond by the house. They hung a left and past right in front of the camera. I got two shots since I was already setup on the tripod. Dennis', '2003-06-02 01:09:44.000000', NULL, 0),
